   1:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c **** /*
   2:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * jcsample.c
   3:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  *
   4:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * Copyright (C) 1991-1996, Thomas G. Lane.
   5:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * This file is part of the Independent JPEG Group's software.
   6:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * For conditions of distribution and use, see the accompanying README file.
   7:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  *
   8:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * This file contains downsampling routines.
   9:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  *
  10:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * Downsampling input data is counted in "row groups".  A row group
  11:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * is defined to be max_v_samp_factor pixel rows of each component,
  12:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * from which the downsampler produces v_samp_factor sample rows.
  13:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * A single row group is processed in each call to the downsampler module.
  14:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  *
  15:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * The downsampler is responsible for edge-expansion of its output data
  16:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * to fill an integral number of DCT blocks horizontally.  The source buffer
  17:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * may be modified if it is helpful for this purpose (the source buffer is
  18:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * allocated wide enough to correspond to the desired output width).
  19:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * The caller (the prep controller) is responsible for vertical padding.
  20:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  *
  21:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * The downsampler may request "context rows" by setting need_context_rows
  22:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * during startup.  In this case, the input arrays will contain at least
  23:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * one row group's worth of pixels above and below the passed-in data;
  24:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * the caller will create dummy rows at image top and bottom by replicating
  25:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * the first or last real pixel row.
  26:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  *
  27:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * An excellent reference for image resampling is
  28:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  *   Digital Image Warping, George Wolberg, 1990.
  29:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  *   Pub. by IEEE Computer Society Press, Los Alamitos, CA. ISBN 0-8186-8944-7.
  30:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  *
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccq7GJi9.s 			page 2


  31:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * The downsampling algorithm used here is a simple average of the source
  32:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * pixels covered by the output pixel.  The hi-falutin sampling literature
  33:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * refers to this as a "box filter".  In general the characteristics of a box
  34:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * filter are not very good, but for the specific cases we normally use (1:1
  35:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * and 2:1 ratios) the box is equivalent to a "triangle filter" which is not
  36:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * nearly so bad.  If you intend to use other sampling ratios, you'd be well
  37:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * advised to improve this code.
  38:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  *
  39:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * A simple input-smoothing capability is provided.  This is mainly intended
  40:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * for cleaning up color-dithered GIF input files (if you find it inadequate,
  41:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * we suggest using an external filtering program such as pnmconvol).  When
  42:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * enabled, each input pixel P is replaced by a weighted sum of itself and its
  43:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * eight neighbors.  P's weight is 1-8*SF and each neighbor's weight is SF,
  44:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * where SF = (smoothing_factor / 1024).
  45:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  * Currently, smoothing is only supported for 2h2v sampling factors.
  46:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c ****  */
  47:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c **** 
  48:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c **** #define JPEG_INTERNALS
  49:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c **** #include "jinclude.h"
  50:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c **** #include "jpeglib.h"
  51:Middlewares/Third_Party/LibJPEG/source/jcsample.c **** 
